A student wants to show that a length of metal wire obeys Ohm's law.
Describe how the student should carry out the experiment and explain how the results show that the wire obeys Ohm's law.
Your answer should include:
• how the meters and the variable resistor are connected, and why;
• how the temperature of the wire is kept constant;
• what is recorded and how the graph is drawn;
• what the graph shows.
This question also assesses the quality of your written communication, including your use of specialist scientific terms.
